<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82705" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεσσός</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεττ-</span></b> , ὁ, heterocl. pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεσσά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					429
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				61
			</span></i> :— <i>oval-shaped stone for playing draughts</i>
			or <i>backgammon</i>, usu. in pl. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκοῖο
				σημήϊα π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.482.21
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>)), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεσσοῖσι . . θυμὸν ἔτερπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.107
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.94
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὶ μὲν ἵπποις . . , τοὶ δὲ πεσσοῖς .
					. τέρπονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					129.4
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεττῶν θέσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					333b
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφηῦρε πεσσοὺς κύβους
			τε</span> (sc. Palamedes) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				479.4
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεις πεσσῶν ὁμοίως διαφοραῖς
				ἐκτις μέναι</span> as if moved from place to place
				like draughts, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				360.9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἒν μὲν τόδ᾽ ἡμῖν, ὥσπερ ἐν
				πεσσοῖς, δίδως κρεῖσσον</span> you have given me <i>a
				piece</i> (as at chess), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				409
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τὸν ἐν πεττοῖς νόμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					987
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεττῶν δίκην τὰς κοινὰς ἐννοίας
					μετατιθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1068c
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν πεττοῖς καὶ κύβοις
				διημερεύειν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				272f
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄζυξ ὢν ὥσπερ ἐν πεττοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1253a7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>the board on which the game was played</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεσσὰ πεντέγραμμα</span>, since the pieces
			were placed on five lines, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				429
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ π</span>. <i>the place</i> in which
			the game was played, or <i>the game itself</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				68
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθα Διὸς . . θᾶκοι π. τε καλοῦνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>medicated plug of wool</i> or <i>lint</i> to be introduced
			into the vagina, anus, etc., <i>pessary</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.20.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.106
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cels.
				5.21
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>any oval body</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐκ μολύβδου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Mith.</u>
					31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>ticket</i> or <i>tally</i> showing attendance at an <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκλησία</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>JHS</u>
				8.118
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Iasus</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>bolt</i> of a door, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Lond.</u>
				121.616
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				2146.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in Archit., <i>cubic mass of building, terrace</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				16.1.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1272.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Aed.</u>
				1.1.37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>dark edge of the pupil</i> (in the eye), <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
